      "writtenOn": "2023-09-27T15:15:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e As `fdt_get_name` returns a `const char*`, you could simply pass its result to `CStr::from_ptr`.\n\n`CStr::from_ptr` is unsafe, and not sure whether it improves readability. Let me keep this as-is.\n\n\n\u003e IIUC, the reason for the extra code is because you\u0027d like to bound-check this with `buffer.get()`, which is a great idea. Could you extract that \"subslicing\" operation into its own `Fdt` method, for re-use (e.g. `.get_from_ptr(const u8*, usize)`?)\n\nDone.\n\nFYI, bound-check with `buffer.get()` is borrowed from existing code :)",
